lisa-design:
- Policy input = HttpResponseData marshalled as JSON, i.e. exactly the JSON the old hand-built evidence carried in status.remarks (status_code, status, headers in Go canonical form, body, response_time_ms, success, error, matched_regex, body_regex_pattern). It matches what plugin-http-collector-policies reads (input.success, input.response_time_ms, input.headers["Content-Type"]); the struct is passed to GenerateResults directly (OPA round-trips it through JSON).
- Labels {provider: http, url, method} seed the policy_manager evidence UUID; method is the upper-cased configured method. Do not add run-varying labels.
- Old props (http_url, http_method, status_code, response_time_ms, success, regex_pattern/regex_matched) are appended to every evidence AFTER GenerateResults, because GenerateResults overwrites Props (with _violation_id props). New prop `error` when no response was received (replaces the old status.reason text).
- Old "HTTP Health Check" activity is passed as the processor's activities (policy_manager appends its own). Old COMPONENT subject (identifier = URL) kept. Actors: the standard CCF + plugin tool actors, like plugin-intruder/plugin-aws-*. Evidence Start/End are overwritten with the request's start/end, as before.
- Request failure (no response: build/send/read-body error): the plugin still evaluates the policies on input {success:false, error, status_code:0}, posts that evidence (ensure_success_status and require_json_content NOT_SATISFIED, like the old NOT_SATISFIED evidence), then returns FAILURE with the error. Rejected: returning FAILURE with no evidence, which would drop the "endpoint down" record operators had. Previously a failed request returned SUCCESS; FAILURE now follows the W2 spec.
- A policy evaluation error returns FAILURE without posting partial evidence (same as plugin-intruder processTarget).
- No policy paths: request is made, no evidence, SUCCESS with a warning log.
- Clock seam (p.now) so the response_time_check violation is tested without a 5 s sleep.
- Fixtures: testdata/policies = the three non-test .rego files copied verbatim from plugin-http-collector-policies@3f4811593af2df92021d9baccb4b43181e6f2fe2 (PR #2, Rego v1). main is Rego v0 and does not parse on the agent's OPA 1.14.1.
